  "title": "What Your Brain Imagines When You're Offline #shorts",
  "description": "Przybylski et al. (2013) built the first fear-of-missing-out scale: people higher in FOMO tended to report lower mood and life satisfaction, used social media more, and were more likely to check it in lectures and while driving (a correlation, not proof of cause). #psychology #shorts #fomo #socialmedia",
